The '''Auster AC-37 Aquilo''' is a Baliscan family of single seat, {{W|twin-engine}}, all-weather [[W:Fifth-generation jet fighter|fifth-generation]] [[W:Multirole combat aircraft|multirole combat aircraft]] that is intended to perform both [[W:Air superiority fighter|air superiority]] and [[W:attack aircraft|strike]] missions. It is also able to provide [[W:Electronic warfare|electronic warfare]] and [[W:Intelligence, surveillance, target acquisition, and reconnaissance#ISR (Intelligence, surveillance and reconnaissance)|intelligence, surveillance, and reconnaissance]] capabilities. The AC-37 is a result of the joint '''Aquilo Development Program''' (''Aquilo'' being [[Baliscano language|Baliscano]] for "wind") between the [[Auster|Auster Corporation]], the prime contractor, and it's principal partners [[BAL Systems]] and the [[Baliscan Aerospace Corporation]], who provided the wings, aft fuselage, avionics integration, and training systems. 

